    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-b63f12a060a0\",\"class\":\"not\",\"constraints\":[],\"coverage\":\"\",\"residual\":\"Do the commit's subject and body accurately describe the main change in its diff, neither claiming something the diff does not do nor omitting its main change?\",\"probes\":null,\"rationale\":\"The rule compares the meaning of the commit message with the meaning of the diff. The contract materialises only the patch, so the subject and body never reach the checker. Even if they did, deciding whether a message accurately describes a change, and what the main change is, is a semantic judgement. Line-level regexes, file globs, imports and egress checks cannot decide that, and no literal form of the rule can be isolated.\"}",
